### SSE answer flow (SseController, /rest/v1)
### No auth required - /rest/** is permitAll (see ResourceServerConfig).
###
### Prerequisite: run one of the "Ask ..." requests in http/question/question.http
### first - it saves conversationId/questionId as GLOBAL variables that the
### requests below reuse.
###
### Real flow: 1) subscribe to SSE, 2) trigger processing (fire-and-forget,
### the actual answer is streamed to the SSE subscription, computed by the
### routing -> agent -> aggregator pipeline), 3) optionally cancel.

### 1. Subscribe to the SSE stream for the question.
### This is a long-lived streaming response (text/event-stream) - keep it
### open (IntelliJ HTTP Client shows incoming events live) or use curl:
###   curl -N {{host}}/rest/v1/sse/subscription/{{conversationId}}/{{questionId}}
GET {{host}}/rest/v1/sse/subscription/{{conversationId}}/{{questionId}}
Accept: text/event-stream

###

### 2. Trigger answer processing - with request #1 still open in another tab/
### terminal, run this to kick off the agent pipeline; the answer is pushed
### to the open SSE subscription rather than returned in this response.
GET {{host}}/rest/v1/sse/question?conversationId={{conversationId}}&questionId={{questionId}}

###

### 3. Cancel a single subscription.
DELETE {{host}}/rest/v1/sse/subscription/{{conversationId}}/{{questionId}}

###

### 4. Cancel a batch of subscriptions in one call.
POST {{host}}/rest/v1/sse/subscriptions/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscriptions": [
    {
      "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
      "questionId": {{questionId}}
    }
  ]
}

###
